Kind: ablation
Issue: #934
Takes out: the reap after the report is queued -- a child is reaped first and its report sent after, as proc_subscribe_exit() does, so a report to a waiter that has gone takes the child with it: musl_test's [40] must see the exec'd image's wait never end, since the child ends after 3 s, with the new image already waiting, and its report goes to the thread the exec took
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: musl_test: \[40\] WRONG -- a waiting thread gone with an exec, and the new image's wait answered -[0-9]+: it did not end in 30 s
Note: Its Expect was "it did NOT find the child's exit", what the new image would have said with a child ending after 500 ms, before its wait.  Since the child ends after 3 s (92cf0d98) the new image is waiting when the child ends, and its wait does not end.  Judged against that Expect under QEMU (TCG and KVM), on OMEGA 10/11/2026 at 92cf0d98 and on omen 15/11/2026 at the union a79ae4d8, it was caught 0 of 4 each time: every ablated boot that reached [40] said its wait did not end in 30 s, seven of eight (the eighth, under TCG, was cut by the 600 s watchdog after [38]); the fixed tree passed 3 of 4 (its fourth trapped in the kernel, outside [40]) and 4 of 4, finding the exit.  The Expect is what those boots said.

